# Version bump on every change

After **any** user-requested change to this project (content, styling, components, config), increment `SITE_VERSION` in `src/lib/version.ts` in the **same commit** as the change.

## Format

- Use `v1.01`, `v1.02`, `v1.03`, … (two-digit patch segment after the dot).
- Do not skip bumps when batching multiple edits in one session.

## Where it appears

`SITE_VERSION` drives the header and under-hero lines via `VersionLine` (`{locationLabel} · {SITE_VERSION}`).

## Workflow

1. Make the requested edits.
2. Bump `SITE_VERSION` in `src/lib/version.ts`.
3. Commit with a message that mentions the new version when pushing to `dev` (unless the user says not to commit/push).

Do not deploy or push unless the user asks (e.g. "push to dev").
